      "verdict": "REJECTED. At strength 0.9 the rendered contrast of the 3:1 lane degrades from 0.723 to 0.857 and the blind pixel detector stops finding it. Brightness in this frame is a density measurement, so any operator that spreads light spatially erases the lanes the page exists to show. Merely having the 24-tap loop compiled into the composite shader, with the strength uniform at zero, cost 0.108 ms of the frame."
    },
    "depthCue": {
      "what": "Any distance-attenuated depth cue, and depth of field.",
      "verdict": "REJECTED on the same evidence, without a separate build. Every available depth cue works by modulating brightness or by spreading it spatially, and brightness is the measurement. The page already has two honest depth cues that touch neither: orbital parallax, and the user-controlled vertical exaggeration slider."
    },
    "lightRigAndIbl": {
      "what": "The full Tier 1 lighting stack: a DirectionalLight with a 2048x2048 PCFSoftShadowMap and a tight frustum, an AmbientLight fill, and scene.environment from the 1k Poly Haven studio_small_09 HDRI (CC0) through PMREMGenerator + RGBELoader.",
